  "assembly_notes": "Four independent structural slots form the complete bucket domain: body profile, mouth-edge construction, swing-bail silhouette and riveted-ear form. The body remains the grounded root and owns the hollow shell, selected rim and paired ears; one swing-bail child always rotates about the real horizontal ear diameter. Mouth size, wall profile, floor/apex closure, rim scale, ear reach, pivot height, wire size and bail rise are derived together for every cross-slot combination. The template emits no bracket, wall plate, cradle, outer support ring, hook mount, full-height structural body hoop, lid, side-grip replacement or separate texture-mark geometry. Finish style and colorway remain non-structural semantic materials.",
